OL,3,CProgramme listings for SUN 10 MAY
OL,4,G1200FPrivate Passions
OL,5,     GMichael Berkeley's guest is 98
OL,6,     Gyear old teacher and writer Joyce
OL,7,     GTrotman.
OL,8,G1330FMusic Map
OL,9,     GSara Mohr-Pietsch explores the
OL,10,     Gwork that famously inspired
OL,11,     GTolstoy, Beethoven's 'Kreutzer'
OL,12,     Gsonata - and asks whether the
OL,13,     Gdedication to the virtuoso
OL,14,     Gviolinst Kreutzer should stand.
OL,15,G1500FMusic Matters: Musical Minds
OL,16,     GPsychotherapist and broadcaster
OL,17,     GNemone Metaxas is joined by
OL,18,     Gpianist Steven Osborne to delve
OL,19,     Ginto our psychological
OL,20,     Grelationship with music and
OL,21,     Guntangle why it means so much to
OL,22,     Gus.
OL,23,Vppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppppp
